WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.925
"I knew she wasn't really a princess," said Jimmy.

2
00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:11.045
The others were silent.

3
00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:15.308
"Can we do anything for you, Mabel?" Gerald asked kindly.

4
00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:18.253
"If not, we should be going."

5
00:00:18.254 --> 00:00:22.880
"Yes, I want my tea," said Jimmy.

6
00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:25.383
"Tea?" Mabel snapped.

7
00:00:25.384 --> 00:00:28.727
"You'd leave me after getting me into this mess?"

8
00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:32.576
"That's unfair!" Gerald began. "We—"

9
00:00:32.577 --> 00:00:36.178
"Leave Mabel alone," interrupted Kathleen.

10
00:00:36.179 --> 00:00:39.457
"It must be horrid to be invisible."

11
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:43.443
"It is. And it's horrid to have an aunt who doesn't like me.

12
00:00:43.444 --> 00:00:47.934
She wouldn't let me go to the fair today because I disobeyed her."

13
00:00:47.935 --> 00:00:52.443
"You'll have to tell her about the ring," said Kathleen.

14
00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:56.429
"No! Take me with you."

15
00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.542
"I suppose you could come home for tea," said Gerald.

16
00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:02.678
"Then we'll decide what to do."

17
00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:06.469
The children agreed that Mabel should leave her aunt a note.

18
00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:09.776
Gerald took out his notebook and pencil.

19
00:01:09.777 --> 00:01:13.804
They watched the pencil move by itself as Mabel wrote:

20
00:01:13.805 --> 00:01:17.259
Dear Aunt, You won't see me again for a while.

21
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.774
A rich lady in an automobile adopted me.

22
00:01:19.775 --> 00:01:21.415
We are going away on a ship.

23
00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:25.543
Don't try to follow me. Mabel

24
00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:29.129
"But that's all lies," said Jimmy.

25
00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:35.135
"If I said I was invisible, she'd think that was a lie too."

26
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:43.371
By the time they arrived home, they were very late for tea.

27
00:01:43.372 --> 00:01:48.680
"Are you all right?" asked Mademoiselle. "I was worried."

28
00:01:48.681 --> 00:01:52.109
"We're sorry," said Gerald.

29
00:01:52.110 --> 00:02:07.130
"Come in," said Mademoiselle. "You'll have supper now."

30
00:02:07.131 --> 00:02:12.218
There were only three plates at the table, so Jimmy let Mabel have his.

31
00:02:12.219 --> 00:02:15.172
He shared with Kathleen.

32
00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:20.521
It was strange to see Mabel's food floating in the air and then disappearing.

33
00:02:20.522 --> 00:02:26.784
Everyone was hungry.

34
00:02:26.785 --> 00:02:31.312
The cook grumbled when she had to bring more food.

35
00:02:31.313 --> 00:02:35.372
"It'll be hard to give Mabel breakfast," said Gerald.

36
00:02:35.373 --> 00:02:38.076
"Mademoiselle will be here then."

37
00:02:38.077 --> 00:02:43.590
"We'll have to buy things and feed her in secret," said Kathleen.

38
00:02:43.591 --> 00:02:47.313
"Our money won't last long," said Jimmy.

39
00:02:47.314 --> 00:02:49.947
"Mabel, do you have any money?"

40
00:02:49.948 --> 00:02:54.418
"No," said Mabel, "but I've got lots of ideas."

41
00:02:54.419 --> 00:02:58.202
That night Kathleen lent Mabel one of her nightgowns.

42
00:02:58.203 --> 00:03:03.957
As Mabel pulled off her princess clothes, they became visible.

43
00:03:03.958 --> 00:03:07.426
As she put on the nightgown, it disappeared.

44
00:03:07.427 --> 00:03:11.290
She and Kathleen soon fell asleep.

45
00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:17.421
The next morning Kathleen woke to find Eliza, the maid, staring at Mabel's princess clothes.

46
00:03:17.422 --> 00:03:19.669
They were piled on a chair.

47
00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.891
"Where on earth did you get those?" asked Eliza.

48
00:03:23.892 --> 00:03:31.213
"Oh . . . oh . . . someone lent them to me for a play we're doing," said Kathleen.

49
00:03:31.214 --> 00:03:34.624
She was saved from saying more by the doorbell.

50
00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:37.263
Eliza hurried away to answer it.

51
00:03:37.264 --> 00:03:43.176
Mabel got up and began to wash her invisible face in the basin.

52
00:03:43.177 --> 00:03:48.628
"I wish you hadn't written such lies to your aunt," said Kathleen.

53
00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:52.486
"What's the use of telling the truth if no one believes you?"

54
00:03:52.487 --> 00:03:55.004
"You should always tell the truth.

55
00:03:55.005 --> 00:03:57.026
Now I'm going to breakfast.

56
00:03:57.027 --> 00:04:03.047
Stay quiet up here, and I'll bring you something to eat."

57
00:04:03.048 --> 00:04:10.477
When Eliza came to make the bed, Mabel untucked the corners of the sheets.

58
00:04:10.478 --> 00:04:14.860
"Drat these sheets!" Eliza exclaimed.

59
00:04:14.861 --> 00:04:18.425
Then Eliza swept the floor.

60
00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:20.930
"Don't forget to sweep under the rugs!"

61
00:04:20.931 --> 00:04:23.334
Mabel whispered in her ear.

62
00:04:23.335 --> 00:04:28.211
Eliza turned white and ran from the room.

63
00:04:28.212 --> 00:04:33.676
Meanwhile Kathleen and Gerald had decided they must tell Mabel's aunt the truth.

64
00:04:33.677 --> 00:04:38.908
So after Mabel's breakfast, the children started walking to the castle.

65
00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:43.036
"Mabel, get behind me," said Kathleen.

66
00:04:43.037 --> 00:04:46.356
"Then our two shadows will look like one."

67
00:04:46.357 --> 00:04:52.910
But as they walked through town, a woman noticed a large, black shape on Kathleen's back.

68
00:04:52.911 --> 00:04:56.063
"Hey, missy!" the woman shouted.

69
00:04:56.064 --> 00:04:58.558
"What have you been leaning against?"

70
00:04:58.559 --> 00:05:05.813
Everyone walked a little faster.

